---
source: crates/sluice-cli/tests/help.rs
expression: "help(&[\"doctor\", \"--help\"])"
---
Check the home, who can reach it, its lock and identity key, and say how to fix a problem

It only reads: it never creates, locks, repairs or deletes anything. The exit code is 0 unless a check failed, and then that of the most serious failure: 6 for policy, 5 for storage. Warnings do not fail.

Usage: sluice doctor [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --json
          Print JSON, one object per line, instead of text. A failure is then a JSON line on stderr

      --network
          Also check the network: whether UDP can be bound, the relay, the public address, the NAT mapping and whether a router can open a port. The plain report stays local and quick

      --color <WHEN>
          When to colour help, errors and other output. NO_COLOR set to anything turns it off

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Colour a stream only when it is a terminal
          - always: Colour always, unless `NO_COLOR` is set
          - never:  Never colour
          
          [default: auto]

      --relay <URL>
          The relay the network checks use and ask for a net report

      --n0-relays
          Use n0's public relays for the network checks (not run by this project)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
